Hi all, we hope you are all recovering from another crazy event that’s happening on our planet earth right now. We are getting active and doing our bit to help raise funds with our upcoming event [Friday Night Party Night on April 1st](https://www.facebook.com/events/264150959236513?ref=newsfeed). All money will be donated to [GIVIT](https://www.givit.org.au/) to help those that have lost everything in the recent floods. Unfortunately it’s been left up to community in Northern NSW to support each other and even save lives in this horrific event. From friends in the local areas of Northern NSW we have heard so much devastation and suffering. Please get on board and help where you can, even if that means a [small donation](https://www.givit.org.au/donate-funds) somewhere. We look forward to seeing you all on April 1st to make this one count!

We are going to have Drum and Dance performances and a free [Afro Pop dance class](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NhAGTR54K4g) to get you all warmed up. We are also going to say goodbye to our dearest friend and dance teacher, Yayoi. She will be heading off to Japan and will be taking a break from teaching our Tuesday night dance classes. She will be sadly missed by all of us and we hope she has an wonderful time in Japan.

We can't wait to see you all there to celebrate, say farewell, and raise funds for those in need. Wear something bright and colourful and bring your family and friends.

Details:

April 1st (No we are not kidding) Palmwoods Memorial Hall, 1 Main St Palmwoods. BYO dinner and drinks. $10 entry for adults (all money is donated to GIVIT for those that have been severely impacted by the floods) 6pm-9pm. Everyone welcome.

Schedule of events:

6pm Arrive

6.30pm Drummers

6.45pm Drum and Dance Performance

7.15pm Djole Circle

7.45pm Bec's Afro Pop Dance Class

8.10pm Afro Pop Dance Off with PRIZES

8.30pm Discoteck - It's Party Time!!

9pm Finish
